<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Output src/sphere.rs. Exact only; num-bigint/num-rational/num-traits already in Cargo.toml; no new dependency, no floating point, no panics on user input (return Option). PiMonomial{coefficient:BigRational,pi_exponent:i32} means coefficient*pi^pi_exponent with multiply, scale, divide(None on zero). exact_rational(n,d)->Option. sphere_monomial_average(exponents:&[u32])->Option<BigRational>: average of prod n_i^e_i over the unit sphere of R^d, d=exponents.len(), uniform probability measure; None for d=0; zero if any exponent odd; else prod (2a_i-1)!!/(d(d+2)...(d+2k-2)), e_i=2a_i, k=sum a_i. unit_sphere_area(d)->Option<PiMonomial>: 2pi^(d/2)/Gamma(d/2) for d>=1 (even d=2m: 2pi^m/(m-1)!; odd d=2m+1: 2*4^m*m!*pi^m/(2m)!). logarithmic_shell_coefficient(d)=area/(2pi)^d. one_loop_inverse_coupling_slope(casimir,gauge_loop_coefficient)=gauge_loop_coefficient*casimir*logarithmic_shell_coefficient(4); doc comment MUST state the action normalization (1/(2g^2))sum_{mu<nu}|F|^2, Killing=-casimir*inner product, and that 11/3 is a textbook input, not derived. Independent tests: tests/sphere_averages.rs (S^3 values 1/4,1/24,1/8; unit-constraint sum rule; areas d=1..6; 11C/(24pi^2); negative controls). Snake_case spelled-out names.
